                <pb facs="0518" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg398"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.01/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Robbins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-04T19:00:00-06:00">January 4, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Department’s telegram January 3, 3 p.m. Minister for Foreign Affairs informs
                    me Government of Salvador takes attitude suggested by the Department and is
                    extending recognition to Reina Andrade as Provisional President.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robbins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
